  "number": "3.1.18",
  "title": "",
  "body": "  The following program has the correct code for linear search, but the code is mixed up. Drag the blocks from the left into the correct order on the right. You will be told if any of the blocks are in the wrong order or are indented incorrectly.     numbers = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50]  found = False  search_value = 100    for number in numbers:    if number == search_value:    found = True  break    if found:    print(\"Found!\")    else:    print(\"Not found.\")    "
